{"author":{"id":"1832e4168d45d4ef31531146dbc743bb950a5dd543b15fd8e3a076fd976bfdef"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791229821,"nonce":"aU+dlJ8cqLF8efYPdj38MNpk5hY=","title":"the generated Haxe drops the declaration's doc comments","message":"A declaration documents its items with `///`, but the Haxe that x-idl writes has no doc comments, so Haxe users never see them. xwindow's api/window.api.rs says which unit each size and position method takes (x()/y() and width() physical, setPosition and setSize logical), and hlwindow's generated Window.hx says nothing; an Ash UI session hit exactly that mismatch.\n\nWanted: each item's `///` text as `/** ... */` above the Haxe declaration it becomes, on both surfaces (HashLink and Rayzor): the public method, the class or abstract, the enum and each of its values, and each record field's setter. Asked for by the xwindow session (xwindow git-bug ca9250431321e1a23d5ddbe5afda6a518df35cb0802011128e3432433845be7e), 2026-10-05.","files":null}]}